rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all runtime-native workflows follow the CAS Execution Model,
    separating orchestration (Runner), reasoning (Workflow), and knowledge access
    (Providers).
  title: Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle) to prevent premature architectural
    promotion.
  title: Pattern and Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all new patterns to be initialized as 'supporting' to ensure validation
    through usage before becoming 'core' foundational elements.
  title: Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the consolidation of patterns across distinct architectural layers
    (e.g., governance vs. execution) to maintain system clarity.
  title: Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that pattern promotion to 'core' status must be supported by evidence
    from multiple sources or systems to ensure architectural stability.
  title: Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work Registry acts as the authoritative source of planning
    state; generated artifacts must derive status from this registry.
  title: Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must use a structured YAML schema instead of
    unstructured text to enable machine processing and UI rendering.
  title: Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must utilize the shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines strict semantic rules for architecture artifacts, distinguishing
    between intent and state, and architect decisions vs. governance-approved system
    state.
  title: Language & Semantics Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures traceability by requiring all patterns derived from heuristics
    to be linked to at least one observed signal as evidence.
  title: Heuristic-Derived Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes the system-wide rule resolution model where Global Rules override
    Project Rules, which in turn override Prompt Rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring all system-proposed architectural
    decisions to be manually accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: System Proposes, Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Governance artifacts generated by the system (AEM, AID) must summarize
    authoritative sources and not become the primary records themselves.
  title: Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Decision Records (ADR) are the sole authoritative source for
    decisions; all metadata and maps must be derived from them.
  title: ADR as Single Source of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory criteria (recurrence, impact, reusability, and stability)
    that a signal must meet before being promoted to a pattern.
  title: Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must be saved as structured ADR files before they
    are permitted to be reflected in maps or other system artifacts.
  title: Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item (e.g., DONE, NEXT) must be
    derived directly from its governance decision status.
  title: Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) acts as a synthesis layer and must
    never contradict the status recorded in Architecture Decision Records.
  title: AEM Consistency with Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are reserved for foundational architectural primitives and
    must not include context-specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
